{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EditingHolds","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other exemption is inferred: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux\/EntityStore\/changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writer’s drained-but-unflushed buffers, and the failed-flush ledger all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"describe writes the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"store","type":"text"}]},{"text":" has seen. A value still sitting in a view’s local","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in none of them, so under","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferRemote"},{"text":" a remote edit can land underneath a half-typed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field and the user’s next keystroke dispatches against a value that changed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out from under them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A hold closes exactly that window, and nothing wider:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["TextEditor(text: $draft)","    .holdsEntity(note.id, in: persistence.editing)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer that modifier — it takes the hold when the editor appears and gives it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"back when the editor goes away, so there is no release to forget. Reach for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/hold(_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/release(_:)"},{"text":" directly only where the editing session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t a view’s lifetime.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"What a hold is not","anchor":"What-a-hold-is-not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A hold ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"defers a remote change; it does not veto one.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Release it and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next merge applies whatever storage holds, including a deletion made","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elsewhere. The worst a leaked hold can do is strand one row at a stale","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value, which is what ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory"},{"text":" does on purpose. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not data loss, and it is not silent either: a merge that actually withheld a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differing value reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/mergeWithheld(entityType:ids:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two alternatives cost less and are often enough. ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.binding(_:sending:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dispatches on write, which makes the value a drained-but-unflushed one and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers it already. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory"},{"text":" exempts a whole collection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"permanently. A hold sits between them: remote-wins stays on everywhere else,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and here only while the user is actually typing.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/init()"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/ids","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/isEmpty"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/hold(_:)","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/isHolding(_:)","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/release(_:)","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/releaseAll()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/